    "engine": "knitr",
    "markdown": "# Roteamento {#sec-m3-roteamento}\n\nRoteamento é calcular o caminho e o custo (distância, tempo) entre pares de pontos sobre uma\nrede. É o que substitui a distância em linha reta do módulo 2 por algo que corresponde ao\ndeslocamento real.\n\nDois pacotes, com perfis distintos:\n\n| | `dodgr` | `r5r` |\n|:--|:--|:--|\n| Implementação | C++ dentro do R | motor R5 (Java) |\n| Modos | um modo por vez (carro, caminhão, a pé, bicicleta) | multimodal, com transporte público e GTFS |\n| Insumo | `sf` de linhas (ex.: OSM) | pasta com `.pbf` + GTFS |\n| Instalação | direta | exige **JDK 21** |\n| Uso típico | rede rodoviária, carga, distâncias | acessibilidade urbana, isócronas |\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nlibrary(sf)\nlibrary(dplyr)\nlibrary(ggplot2)\n\n# mapa-base padrão dos mapview(): OpenStreetMap\nmapview::mapviewOptions(basemaps = c(\"OpenStreetMap\", \"CartoDB.Positron\", \"Esri.WorldImagery\"))\n```\n:::\n\n\n## `dodgr`: roteamento sobre a malha viária\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nlibrary(dodgr)\n\n# 1. a malha: vias principais do corredor Curitiba–Paranaguá, a mesma do @sec-m3-osm\n#    (para um estado inteiro, troque por osmextract::oe_get(), como lá)\narquivo_rede <- \"dados/brutos/rede_curitiba_paranagua.gpkg\"\n\nif (!file.exists(arquivo_rede)) {\n  res <- osmdata::opq(bbox = c(-49.35, -25.62, -48.45, -25.35), timeout = 180) |>\n    osmdata::add_osm_feature(key = \"highway\", value = c(\n      \"motorway\", \"motorway_link\", \"trunk\", \"trunk_link\", \"primary\", \"primary_link\",\n      \"secondary\", \"secondary_link\", \"tertiary\")) |>\n    osmdata::osmdata_sf()\n\n  res$osm_lines |>\n    dplyr::select(dplyr::any_of(c(\"osm_id\", \"name\", \"ref\", \"highway\", \"maxspeed\",\n                                  \"oneway\", \"lanes\"))) |>\n    sf::st_write(arquivo_rede, quiet = TRUE)\n}\n\nrede <- sf::st_read(arquivo_rede, quiet = TRUE) |>\n  dplyr::rename(geometry = geom)\n\n# 2. construir o grafo com um perfil de peso\ngrafo <- dodgr::weight_streetnet(rede, wt_profile = \"motorcar\", type_col = \"highway\")\n\n# 3. componente conectado principal (descarta trechos isolados)\ngrafo <- grafo[grafo$component == 1, ]\n\n# 4. matriz de distâncias entre pontos: centro de Curitiba e Porto de Paranaguá\norigens  <- cbind(x = c(-49.2733, -48.5119), y = c(-25.4284, -25.5016))   # lon, lat\ndestinos <- origens\n\ndodgr::dodgr_dists(grafo, from = origens, to = destinos)      # metros\n#>          15986    56663\n#> 15986     0.00 93852.59\n#> 56663 95230.78     0.00\ndodgr::dodgr_times(grafo, from = origens, to = destinos)      # segundos\n#>          15986    56663\n#> 15986    0.000 4003.341\n#> 56663 4313.666    0.000\n```\n:::\n\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\n# o caminho em si, como geometria, para desenhar no mapa\ncaminho <- dodgr::dodgr_paths(grafo, from = origens[1, , drop = FALSE],\n                       to = origens[2, , drop = FALSE])\n\nverts <- dodgr::dodgr_vertices(grafo)\nrota <- verts[match(caminho[[1]][[1]], verts$id), c(\"x\", \"y\")] |>\n  as.matrix() |>\n  sf::st_linestring() |>\n  sf::st_sfc(crs = 4326)\n```\n:::\n\n\nA conferência visual, como sempre: a rota deve seguir a BR-277 descendo a serra.\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nextremos <- data.frame(nome = c(\"Curitiba\", \"Paranaguá\"),\n                       lon = origens[, 1], lat = origens[, 2]) |>\n  sf::st_as_sf(coords = c(\"lon\", \"lat\"), crs = 4326)\n\nmapview::mapview(rota, color = \"#b3402a\", lwd = 5, layer.name = \"Rota\") +\n  mapview::mapview(extremos, col.regions = \"#1a5b8a\", layer.name = \"Origem e destino\")\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"leaflet html-widget html-fill-item\" id=\"htmlwidget-84a5b54712904bcf6cb0\" style=\"width:100%;height:406px;\"></div>\n<script type=\"application/json\" data-for=\"htmlwidget-84a5b54712904bcf6cb0\">{\"x\":{\"options\":{\"minZoom\":1,\"maxZoom\":52,\"crs\":{\"crsClass\":\"L.CRS.EPSG3857\",\"code\":null,\"proj4def\":null,\"projectedBounds\":null,\"options\":{}},\"preferCanvas\":false,\"bounceAtZoomLimits\":false,\"maxBounds\":[[[-90,-370]],[[90,370]]]},\"calls\":[{\"method\":\"addProviderTiles\",\"args\":[\"OpenStreetMap\",\"OpenStreetMap\",\"OpenStreetMap\",{\"errorTileUrl\":\"\",\"noWrap\":false,\"detectRetina\":false,\"pane\":\"tilePane\"}]},{\"method\":\"addProviderTiles\",\"args\":[\"CartoDB.Positron\",\"CartoDB.Positron\",\"CartoDB.Positron\",{\"errorTileUrl\":\"\",\"noWrap\":false,\"detectRetina\":false,\"pane\":\"tilePane\"}]},{\"method\":\"addProviderTiles\",\"args\":[\"Esri.WorldImagery\",\"Esri.WorldImagery\",\"Esri.WorldImagery\",{\"errorTileUrl\":\"\",\"noWrap\":false,\"detectRetina\":false,\"pane\":\"tilePane\"}]},{\"method\":\"createMapPane\",\"args\":[\"line\",430]},{\"method\":\"addPolylines\",\"args\":[[[[{\"lng\":[-49.2732084,-49.2733995,-49.2736203,-49.2736327,-49.2736368,-49.273634,-49.2735498,-49.2734915,-49.2734293,-49.2729107,-49.2723615,-49.2719819,-49.2719023,-49.2718206,-49.2717714,-49.2717334,-49.2707591,-49.2702912,-49.2694758,-49.268563,-49.2684856,-49.2670499,-49.2660294,-49.26593,-49.2658808,-49.2658718,-49.2657749,-49.2648512,-49.2647655,-49.2646594,-49.2641493,-49.264101,-49.2639866,-49.2633248,-49.2632091,-49.2625823,-49.2622885,-49.2621935,-49.2620766,-49.2619151,-49.2618473,-49.2616289,-49.2596426,-49.259529,-49.2591498,-49.2590312,-49.2589884,-49.2588901,-49.2585345,-49.258242,-49.2580989,-49.258066,-49.2580381,-49.257698,-49.2576785,-49.2576277,-49.2569286,-49.2568471,-49.2567094,-49.2566577,-49.2565765,-49.2557714,-49.2556735,-49.2554577,-49.2554424,-49.2552386,-49.2551605,-49.2551043,-49.2550507,-49.254897,-49.2547824,-49.2547397,-49.2546978,-49.2546353,-49.2545591,-49.2544806,-49.2544122,-49.2543244,-49.2542425,-49.2541533,-49.2540533,-49.2539476,-49.2538265,-49.2537115,-49.253625,-49.2535175,-49.2534288,-49.2533275,-49.2527553,-49.2526712,-49.2525975,-49.2525174,-49.2524282,-49.2522947,-49.2522022,-49.2520796,-49.251983,-49.251408,